## IMPORTANT SCENARIOS :
------------------------

SCENARIO 1: TIER CHANGE CONFLICT
---------------------------------

Admin FREE rule ko PREMIUM me change karna chahta hai, but already PREMIUM rule exists → 409 Conflict. 
Admin ko pehle PREMIUM rule delete karna padega.


SCENARIO 2: DELETE ACTIVE RULE — COUNTERS KA KYA?
--------------------------------------------------

- Rule cache (Local + Rules Redis): Immediately delete karo — DEL rule:{rule_id}. Stale rule use nahi hona chahiye.

- Counters Redis: Immediately delete mat karo — TTL expire hone do.
  
  Situation:

   a) Original rule: limit = 100/min
   b) User ne 50 requests ki → counter = 50, bache 50
   c) Admin rule delete + recreate with limit = 150 (limit badha di)
   d) Counter bhi delete ho gaya → counter = 0 (fresh)
   e) User ne 150 aur requests bheji → counter 0 se 150 → saari allow
   f) Actual total same window me: 50 (purane) + 150 (naye) = 200 requests
   g) Expected total: 150 (new limit) → user ko sirf 100 aur milne chahiye the (150 - 50, kyunki 50 already use ho chuke)
   h) Result: Limit 150 hai, but user ne 200 kar liye → 50 extra allow — limit violation.
   i) Solution: Counter ko TTL expire hone do (max = window_seconds). Rule recreate ya restore ho jaaye mid-window to old counter 
      still available → sahi enforcement hoti hai.



SCENARIO 3: CRITICAL RULE DELETE —> 2 PERSON APPROVAL
------------------------------------------------------



SCENARIO 4: UPDATE CONSISTENCY ACROSS INSTANCES
------------------------------------------------

DB write ke baad Rule Service rule update ka event publish karti hai Kafka topic me. Do failure scenarios handle karne hain:

a) Kafka Down Hai -  Transactional Outbox Pattern use karenge (already discussed)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

b) Consumer Instance Hi Down Hai
----------------------------------

Case 1: Same consumer restart (same consumer group ID)

- Wo apne last committed offset ke baad se reading resume karta hai — jisse uske down hone ke baad broadcast huye events
  bhi use mil jaate hain, koi event miss nahi hota.

Case 2: Naya instance spin up (naya dynamic consumer group ID)

- Naye group ID ke liye koi committed offset exist nahi karta. Is case me auto.offset.reset decide karta hai ki reading kahan se start ho:

   —> earliest → consumer topic ke start se saare events process karega. Ye redundant hai kyunki wo events already pichle consumer instance ne process kar diye the.
   —> latest (recommended) → consumer sirf future events receive karega — matlab last missed event kabhi process nahi hoga.

- Lekin latest me missed event koi problem create nahi karta kyunki Naya instance ka Local Cache empty hai and rule Redis already rule service ne populate / update
  kar diya hoga. Naya instance ki pehli request pe: Local Cache MISS → Redis HIT (already fresh) → serve ho jaayega. DB tabhi jaayega jab Redis bhi miss ho.





======================================================
# RATE LIMITER — RATE LIMIT ENFORCEMENT APIs DESIGN
======================================================

Humare setup me rate limiting embedded hai — koi public rate-limit check endpoint nahi hai.

API Gateway level — global per-user limit (filter/middleware ke through)
Service level — per-user-per-service + per-user-per-service-per-endpoint (service ke andar filter)


---------------------
1. RESPONSE HEADERS 
---------------------

Har business API ke response me — 200 aur 429 dono — ye headers bhejo:

Header	                   Value	        Kab bhejna
X-RateLimit-Limit	         100          	Har response (200 + 429) — total allowed limit
X-RateLimit-Remaining	     42	            Har response (200 + 429) — bachi hui requests
X-RateLimit-Reset	         1728000060	    Har response (200 + 429) — Unix timestamp, kab window reset hogi
Retry-After	               30	            Sirf 429 — kitne seconds baad retry karna hai


## NOTE :
----------
Gateway global headers set karta hai and service ko forward karta hai → respective service apni values calculate karti hai aur existing 
header value se compare karti hai — agar uski X-RateLimit-Remaining chhoti hai to hi overwrite karti hai → endpoint bhi same tarah
compare-and-replace karta hai → final headers me wo layer jeetti hai jiska X-RateLimit-Remaining minimum hai — kyunki wahi actual 
bottleneck hai jo pehle 429 trigger karega. Yehi signal client ko chahiye taaki wo proactively back off kar sake.


